From 511b0b46e1212dc9003fec07a15641424351db82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 02:31:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/36] EmbeddedWebView: force QStringBuilder materialization
 in custom-CSS URL

(myColors + m_customCss).toUtf8() doesn't compile on Qt4: QStringBuilder
has no toUtf8() member there (apparently Qt5 grew enough QString-mirroring
convenience methods on QStringBuilder over time that this worked without
forcing materialization first -- Qt4's is more limited). Wrapped the
concatenation in QString(...) so .toUtf8() runs on a real QString.

Also pre-emptively fixed the outer QByteArray + QByteArray chain feeding
QString::fromUtf8() the same way the cClient() macro and
ComposerAttachments.cpp needed -- wrapped in QByteArray(...) before the
fromUtf8() call, since that's the same raw-pointer-conversion pattern
that already failed once nested builders were involved.

Swept src/ for the same shape (a member function called directly on an
unmaterialized (a + b) parenthesized expression) -- no other real
instances; several regex hits were plain int arithmetic (i+1, ++i) or
already-safe cases already wrapped in a constructor call.
---
 src/Gui/EmbeddedWebView.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Gui/EmbeddedWebView.cpp b/src/Gui/EmbeddedWebView.cpp
index 40a85e95..4c196fca 100644
--- a/src/Gui/EmbeddedWebView.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/EmbeddedWebView.cpp
@@ -399,7 +399,7 @@ void EmbeddedWebView::addCustomStylesheet(const QString &css)
 
     const QString urlPrefix(QStringLiteral("data:text/css;charset=utf-8;base64,"));
     const QString myColors(QStringLiteral("body { background-color: %1; color: %2; }\n").arg(bgName, fgName));
-    s->setUserStyleSheetUrl(QString::fromUtf8(urlPrefix.toUtf8() + (myColors + m_customCss).toUtf8().toBase64()));
+    s->setUserStyleSheetUrl(QString::fromUtf8(QByteArray(urlPrefix.toUtf8() + QString(myColors + m_customCss).toUtf8().toBase64())));
 }
 
 }
